by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-16T08:53:14Z

Rebased on 8.2 and pushed a few fixes:

* `fragment_renderer.php` referenced the renderer as a string, with a comment saying this avoided triggering the deprecation. It does not: the deprecation is triggered by the constructor, so `::class` and reflection stay silent. Restored the import.
* The changelog and upgrade entries announced the `fragment.renderer.hinclude.global_template` parameter as deprecated, but nothing deprecated it. It is deprecated now. The extension inlines the value into the service argument so the parameter is never resolved at compile time, which means enabling `framework.fragments` does not trigger the deprecation by itself. Same shape as the `router.request_context.*` deprecation in 8.1.
* Removed a stray comma inside the `render_hinclude()` replacement text.
* Added tests for the parameter deprecation and for the case that must stay silent.

I also rewrote the description to list the deprecated surface and to be explicit that the replacements are not equivalent: `render_esi()` and `render()` move composition to the server, and only UX Turbo keeps the non-blocking client-side loading. That distinction should make it into the docs.

@fabpot your review asked for the 8.1 to 8.2 retarget, which was applied back in August, so this only needs a fresh look.
